RETROACTIVE LOG — commit e19f2cd, recorded after the fact (the changelog/ convention
was introduced later, in commit 478c817).

File: vUX-spaEngine.js

=======================================================================
Section 1 — getDynamicData(): pattern segment capture
OLD_SECTION
if (segmentIsData(patternSegments[x])){
    state.data[x+1] = routeSegments[x];
}else if (routeSegments[x] != patternSegments[x]) {
    state.status = false;
    break;
}

NEW_SECTION
if (segmentIsData(patternSegments[x])){
    // ";name" captures the segment, ";name:regex" validates it against the regex first
    let spec            = patternSegments[x].slice(1);
    let separatorIndex  = spec.indexOf(":");
    let name            = separatorIndex == -1 ? spec : spec.slice(0, separatorIndex);
    let segmentPattern  = separatorIndex == -1 ? null : spec.slice(separatorIndex + 1);

    if (segmentPattern != null && !(new RegExp(segmentPattern)).test(routeSegments[x])){
        state.status = false;
        break;
    }

    state.data[name != "" ? name : x+1] = routeSegments[x];
}else if (routeSegments[x] != patternSegments[x]) {
    state.status = false;
    break;
}

REASON
Route params were only captured positionally (data[2] = "7"). ";name" and
";name:regex" segments now capture params by name and optionally validate them, with
the legacy ":regex" form staying positional for compatibility.

=======================================================================
Section 2 — callbacks receive route data
OLD_SECTION
usedHistoryCallback(element, routeName, callbackKey)
usedloadCallBack(element, routeName, callbackKey)          (three call sites)
bootCallback(routeProperties.name)

NEW_SECTION
usedHistoryCallback(element, routeName, callbackKey, routeProperties.data)
usedloadCallBack(element, routeName, callbackKey, routeProperties.data)
bootCallback(routeProperties.name, routeProperties.data)

REASON
The captured route params were never handed to consumer code; they are now passed as
the last argument to bootCallback, clickLoadCallbacks, historyCallbacks and the
clickLoadCallback fallback.

=======================================================================
Section 3 — saveState(): history URL
OLD_SECTION
let path = routeConfigs.routes[routeName].path;

NEW_SECTION
//push the actual requested route so dynamic URLs (e.g "/user/7") survive in the address bar
let path = routeProperties.route != undefined ? routeProperties.route : routeConfigs.routes[routeName].path;

(routeProperties gains a `route` field at both construction sites, holding the
actual requested route, e.g "/user/7" for the pattern "/user/;id".)

REASON
history.pushState stored the configured path literal (e.g "/user/;id"), so refreshing
or bookmarking a dynamic route broke; the real requested URL is now preserved.
